{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. No top-level data variable is conditioned on with a sampling statement; `N_heights`, `heights`, and `N_drops` are context inputs used only for generated quantities.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program contains no model-block likelihood terms, no parameters requiring priors, and no forbidden direct target manipulation.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  real t_fall(real g, real h) {
    return sqrt(2 * h / g);
  }
}

data {
  int N_heights;
  array[N_heights] real<lower=0> heights; // meters
  int N_drops;
}

generated quantities {
  real<lower=0> sigma_t = abs(normal_rng(0, 0.5));
  real<lower=0> g = inv_gamma_rng(1.49, 2.83);

  array[N_drops, N_heights] real mu_t_fall;
  array[N_drops, N_heights] real obs_t_fall;

  for (n in 1:N_drops) {
    for (h in 1:N_heights) {
      mu_t_fall[n, h] = t_fall(g, heights[h]);
      obs_t_fall[n, h] = normal_rng(mu_t_fall[n, h], sigma_t);
    }
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N_drops":5,"N_heights":3,"heights":[4.185359043840389,0.1974802048343865,3.1783236155335604]}","protected_variables":[]}
